Deprecation notices are an important part of making the transition to new code as painless as possible for users. Here's a template you can customize for your own project:
```
/// [DEPRECATED] 
/// Reason: [BRIEFLY EXPLAIN WHY IT'S BEING DEPRECATED]
/// Suggested Replacement: [OPTIONAL - SUGGEST REPLACEMENT CODE]
///
/// 
/// Note: This function/subroutine will be removed after 
/// [DATE]. Any use of it will result in a warning.
///
/// [e.g. Here's example usage]
/// 
/// [NEW FUNCTION NAME](new_function_param) {
///   // Function code here
/// }
```
And when you're done, you can adapt this template to your coding style and project. For example, if your code has a lot of JSDoc comments, you'd want to use that style, otherwise you'd use the natural language comment form. The goal is to plan ahead and leave behind clear directions for your users that'll help them avoid future bugs. Do you want me to help write your own deprecation notice? What's the function/subroutine you're deprecating, and what's the reason for it? Want me to suggest any replacement code?
